    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first post office opened a mile south of the village in a general store owned by Mr. Cox, with Thomas Jay as postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://pleasanthillhistorycenter.com/pleasant_hill",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Samuel Coate built the first house in the new town, a small frame building that doubled as a store and home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://pleasanthillhistorycenter.com/pleasant_hill",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Abraham Whitmer was the first blacksmith in Pleasant Hill, while John Howard had already been known as a blacksmith in the county by 1837.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://pleasanthillhistorycenter.com/pleasant_hill",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "David Patty arrived in 1820 and practiced medicine in Pleasant Hill for twenty years, becoming a respected local physician.",
